@* Accordion (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/navigation.css</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A collapsible section built on the native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> elements, so it opens
    and closes without JavaScript. Consecutive accordions are separated by a line.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <details class="dnf-accordion" open>
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Advanced</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel">
            <p>Custom CSS class, cache lifetime and the canonical URL of the page.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="dnf-accordion">
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Revisions</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel">
            <p>The last 20 saved versions of the page.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="with-fields" title="Optional settings" description="Advanced settings tucked away in a card; the fields inside stay real form controls." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-card">
        <div class="dnf-card__body">
            <details class="dnf-accordion">
                <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">SMTP options</summary>
                <div class="dnf-accordion__panel dnf-form">
                    <div class="dnf-field">
                        <label class="dnf-field__label" for="accordion-timeout">Timeout (seconds)</label>
                        <input class="dnf-input" id="accordion-timeout" type="number" value="30" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="dnf-field">
                        <label class="dnf-field__label" for="accordion-helo">HELO name</label>
                        <input class="dnf-input" id="accordion-helo" value="cms.example.com" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="exclusive" title="One open at a time" description="Native details elements sharing a name attribute form a group in which the browser keeps only one open." layout="block">
    <details class="dnf-accordion" name="docs-faq" open>
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Who can publish a page?</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>Editors and administrators; authors can save drafts.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="dnf-accordion" name="docs-faq">
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Where are uploads stored?</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>In the configured file storage - a folder on disk or an S3 bucket.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="dnf-accordion" name="docs-faq">
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Can I restore an old version?</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>Yes, from the page's revisions.</p></div>
    </details>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="with-badge" title="Rich trigger" description="The trigger is a flex row: an icon or a badge can follow the text." layout="block">
    <details class="dnf-accordion">
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Failed deliveries <span class="dnf-badge dnf-badge--danger">3</span></summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>The endpoint answered 500 at 09:12, 09:14 and 09:20.</p></div>
    </details>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="Utilities on the trigger beat its small muted text - a section title that reads like a heading." layout="block">
    <details class="dnf-accordion" open>
        <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger text-base text-foreground">Danger zone</summary>
        <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>Delete the site's content and start over.</p></div>
    </details>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="Unlayered CSS restyles the parts in a scope - here an indented panel." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-accordion">
        <details class="dnf-accordion" open>
            <summary class="dnf-accordion__trigger">Headers</summary>
            <div class="dnf-accordion__panel"><p>Content-Type: application/json</p></div>
        </details>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-accordion .dnf-accordion__panel {
    padding-inline-start: var(--dnf-space-4);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-accordion</code></td><td>block</td><td>the <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>; consecutive accordions are separated by a line</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-accordion__trigger</code></td><td>element</td><td>the <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code>: muted semibold <code>text-sm</code> with a chevron (<code>::before</code>), no native marker</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-accordion__panel</code></td><td>element</td><td>the content, <code>--dnf-space-3</code> below</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>open</td><td><code>[open]</code></td><td>the chevron turns down (animated)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>hover</td><td><code>.dnf-accordion__trigger:hover</code></td><td>foreground colour</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There is no tag helper and no script: the classes on native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> are the
    API. <code>open</code> opens a section initially.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Native: the summary is a button-like control (Enter and Space) and its open state is announced.</li>
    <li>Put a heading inside the summary if the section needs one in the page outline.</li>
    <li>The chevron is decorative; the open state comes from the native element, not from the drawing.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use it for optional or advanced settings.</li>
    <li>Don't hide required fields in a closed accordion.</li>
    <li>Don't use it to switch between alternatives - that is <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/tabs">tabs</a>.</li>
</ul>
